// ADR 16.10.26g: both compilers print the same `check` line. A theorem citing
// an axiom one hop (`bad2`), two hops (`bad3`) or through a program definition
// (`bad4` via `via_fn`) rests on it; `uses_fine` cites a real proof and does
// not. Axiom-only, because an axiom is the only hole the self-host accepts.

axiom ax(): Void
theorem bad2(): Void { ax() }
theorem bad3(): Void { bad2() }
fn via_fn() -> Void { ax() }
theorem bad4(): Void { via_fn() }
theorem fine(): 1 == 1 { refl }
theorem uses_fine(): 1 == 1 { fine() }
